{
  "suite": "auth-phone",
  "note": [
    "The flows that need a telephone. Phone sign in is off in a Supabase project that has changed nothing, the auth suite is recorded against a project that has changed nothing, and so every phone endpoint there is a refusal and the refusals are cases in it already. Everything past them needs the provider on, a provider is a property of a server rather than of a request, and a suite is asked against one server. So this is a suite of its own rather than a handful of cases in the one next door.",
    "The reference is the same GoTrue 2.195.0 in the same configuration, in a database of its own, with GOTRUE_EXTERNAL_PHONE_ENABLED=true, a Twilio provider, and GOTRUE_SMS_TEST_OTP naming the ten numbers below. zou is told the same thing by 'sms' here, and those two settings are the whole difference between this suite's targets and the auth suite's.",
    "Nothing here can read an sms, so every number this suite uses has its code written down on both servers. That is a real GoTrue feature rather than a hole cut for the harness: a number on the list is never texted, gets the code next to it, and the code is what a verify for that number is checked against whether or not one was ever asked for. So no provider is ever called, the credentials both sides carry are not credentials, and a case can send the code the server is about to expect.",
    "The numbers are all in 555 0100 through 555 0199, the range set aside so that nothing in a test can ring somebody's telephone.",
    "Two people are seeded, both of them a phone and nothing else, because that is what an account made by a phone signup looks like. Everything a case needs beyond those two it makes for itself, which is why most of the file is chains: a number can only be changed by somebody who is signed in, and a resend can only be refused as too soon if something was sent first.",
    "Neither side has the wait between codes turned off. A minute is what a project that changed nothing has, it is what the reference is on, and so the case that asks for a second code inside that minute is recorded as being told to wait rather than being run against a server that would not have said so.",
    "The values that cannot be the same twice are named in 'volatile' and compared as the shape they had. Everything else is compared byte for byte."
  ],
  "schemas": ["public"],
  "sms": {
    "provider": "twilio",
    "test_otp": {
      "15550100000": "313370",
      "15550100001": "424242",
      "15550100002": "151515",
      "15550100003": "262626",
      "15550100004": "373737",
      "15550100005": "484848",
      "15550100006": "595959",
      "15550100007": "606060",
      "15550100008": "717171",
      "15550100009": "828282"
    }
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "what a sign in screen reads when a number is a way in",
      "feature": "settings",
      "path": "/auth/v1/settings",
      "key": "anon",
      "note": "the same read as in the auth suite, against a server with the provider on, so that a client which draws a phone field off this answer is drawing it off something that was measured"
    },

    {
      "name": "somebody signs up with a number and a password",
      "feature": "signup.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/signup",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100001\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\"}",
      "writes": true,
      "note": "no session in the answer, because the number is not confirmed yet. What comes back is the account, and the code went to the telephone",
      "volatile": [
        "/id",
        "/created_at",
        "/updated_at",
        "/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/user_metadata/sub",
        "/identities/0/identity_id",
        "/identities/0/id",
        "/identities/0/user_id",
        "/identities/0/identity_data/sub",
        "/identities/0/last_sign_in_at",
        "/identities/0/created_at",
        "/identities/0/updated_at"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "the code that number was sent",
      "feature": "verify.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100001\",\"token\":\"424242\"}",
      "chained": true,
      "holds": {"token": "body:/access_token"},
      "volatile": [
        "/access_token",
        "/refresh_token",
        "/expires_at",
        "/user/id",
        "/user/created_at",
        "/user/updated_at",
        "/user/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/confirmed_at",
        "/user/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/user/phone_confirmed_at",
        "/user/user_metadata/sub",
        "/user/identities/0/identity_id",
        "/user/identities/0/id",
        "/user/identities/0/user_id",
        "/user/identities/0/identity_data/sub",
        "/user/identities/0/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/identities/0/created_at",
        "/user/identities/0/updated_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/user/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "what the account that proved its number looks like to itself",
      "feature": "user.phone",
      "path": "/auth/v1/user",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"authorization": "Bearer {token}"},
      "chained": true,
      "volatile": [
        "/id",
        "/created_at",
        "/updated_at",
        "/last_sign_in_at",
        "/confirmed_at",
        "/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/phone_confirmed_at",
        "/user_metadata/sub",
        "/identities/0/identity_id",
        "/identities/0/id",
        "/identities/0/user_id",
        "/identities/0/identity_data/sub",
        "/identities/0/last_sign_in_at",
        "/identities/0/created_at",
        "/identities/0/updated_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/factors"]
    },

    {
      "name": "a written code for a number nobody sent one to",
      "feature": "verify.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100000\",\"token\":\"313370\"}",
      "writes": true,
      "note": "the seeded person was never sent one, and the answer is a session all the same. A number whose code was written down is checked against what was written, because nothing was ever drawn for it, so there is no column holding a code and no minute for one to run out in",
      "volatile": [
        "/access_token",
        "/refresh_token",
        "/expires_at",
        "/user/updated_at",
        "/user/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/confirmed_at",
        "/user/phone_confirmed_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/user/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "a code that is not the one",
      "feature": "verify.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100000\",\"token\":\"000000\"}",
      "writes": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a code for a number nobody has",
      "feature": "verify.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100009\",\"token\":\"828282\"}",
      "writes": true,
      "note": "the code is the written one and the answer is still a refusal, in the same words as a wrong code: the list decides what a number's code is, not whether the number has an account"
    },
    {
      "name": "a code with no number to check it against",
      "feature": "verify.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"token\":\"313370\"}"
    },

    {
      "name": "signing in with a number and a password",
      "feature": "token.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100000\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\"}",
      "writes": true,
      "volatile": [
        "/access_token",
        "/refresh_token",
        "/expires_at",
        "/user/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/updated_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/user/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "the wrong password for a number",
      "feature": "token.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100000\",\"password\":\"not-the-password\"}",
      "writes": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a number nobody has, with a password",
      "feature": "token.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100009\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\"}",
      "note": "the same words as the wrong password, for the same reason as the verify pair above"
    },
    {
      "name": "a number written the way a telephone shows it",
      "feature": "token.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"+1 (555) 010-0000\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\"}",
      "writes": true,
      "note": "the punctuation a person types is not the digits a row holds, and what a server does with the difference is the whole of this case"
    },

    {
      "name": "asking for a code by telephone",
      "feature": "otp.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/otp",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100000\"}",
      "writes": true
    },
    {
      "name": "spending the code that asked for",
      "feature": "verify.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100000\",\"token\":\"313370\"}",
      "chained": true,
      "holds": {"signed_in": "body:/access_token"},
      "volatile": [
        "/access_token",
        "/refresh_token",
        "/expires_at",
        "/user/updated_at",
        "/user/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/confirmed_at",
        "/user/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/user/phone_confirmed_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/user/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "moving to another number",
      "feature": "user.phone_change",
      "method": "PUT",
      "path": "/auth/v1/user",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {
        "content-type": "application/json",
        "authorization": "Bearer {signed_in}"
      },
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100004\"}",
      "chained": true,
      "note": "the number does not move here. What moves is new_phone, and the account keeps the old one until the code that went to the new one comes back",
      "volatile": [
        "/updated_at",
        "/last_sign_in_at",
        "/confirmed_at",
        "/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/phone_confirmed_at",
        "/phone_change_sent_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "the code the new number was sent",
      "feature": "verify.phone_change",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"phone_change\",\"phone\":\"15550100004\",\"token\":\"373737\"}",
      "chained": true,
      "volatile": [
        "/access_token",
        "/refresh_token",
        "/expires_at",
        "/user/updated_at",
        "/user/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/confirmed_at",
        "/user/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/user/phone_confirmed_at",
        "/user/phone_change_sent_at",
        "/user/identities/0/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/identities/0/updated_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/user/factors"]
    },

    {
      "name": "asking for a code for a number nobody has",
      "feature": "otp.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/otp",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100002\"}",
      "writes": true,
      "note": "an account is made for it, which is what a phone otp does when nobody says otherwise"
    },
    {
      "name": "the code that made an account",
      "feature": "verify.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100002\",\"token\":\"151515\"}",
      "chained": true,
      "volatile": [
        "/access_token",
        "/refresh_token",
        "/expires_at",
        "/user/id",
        "/user/created_at",
        "/user/updated_at",
        "/user/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/confirmed_at",
        "/user/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/user/phone_confirmed_at",
        "/user/user_metadata/sub",
        "/user/identities/0/identity_id",
        "/user/identities/0/id",
        "/user/identities/0/user_id",
        "/user/identities/0/identity_data/sub",
        "/user/identities/0/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/identities/0/created_at",
        "/user/identities/0/updated_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/user/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "asking for a code for a number nobody has, without making an account",
      "feature": "otp.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/otp",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100003\",\"create_user\":false}",
      "writes": true
    },
    {
      "name": "asking for a code with no number and no address",
      "feature": "otp.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/otp",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{}",
      "writes": true
    },

    {
      "name": "a signup nobody finished",
      "feature": "resend.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/signup",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100005\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\"}",
      "writes": true,
      "volatile": [
        "/id",
        "/created_at",
        "/updated_at",
        "/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/user_metadata/sub",
        "/identities/0/identity_id",
        "/identities/0/id",
        "/identities/0/user_id",
        "/identities/0/identity_data/sub",
        "/identities/0/last_sign_in_at",
        "/identities/0/created_at",
        "/identities/0/updated_at"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "sending the code again a moment after the signup",
      "feature": "resend.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/resend",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100005\"}",
      "chained": true,
      "note": "inside the minute a number waits between codes, so the answer is how long is left rather than a second code. The number in the message is the whole of what a client shows somebody"
    },
    {
      "name": "the code the signup sent, after the resend was refused",
      "feature": "resend.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/verify",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100005\",\"token\":\"484848\"}",
      "chained": true,
      "volatile": [
        "/access_token",
        "/refresh_token",
        "/expires_at",
        "/user/id",
        "/user/created_at",
        "/user/updated_at",
        "/user/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/confirmed_at",
        "/user/confirmation_sent_at",
        "/user/phone_confirmed_at",
        "/user/user_metadata/sub",
        "/user/identities/0/identity_id",
        "/user/identities/0/id",
        "/user/identities/0/user_id",
        "/user/identities/0/identity_data/sub",
        "/user/identities/0/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/identities/0/created_at",
        "/user/identities/0/updated_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/user/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "sending the code again to a number with nothing outstanding",
      "feature": "resend.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/resend",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"type\":\"sms\",\"phone\":\"15550100000\"}",
      "writes": true
    },
    {
      "name": "sending again with no type",
      "feature": "resend.sms",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/resend",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100000\"}",
      "writes": true
    },

    {
      "name": "a number somebody already has",
      "feature": "signup.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/signup",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100000\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\"}",
      "writes": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a number that is not one",
      "feature": "signup.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/signup",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"not-a-number\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\"}",
      "writes": true
    },
    {
      "name": "a number with no password",
      "feature": "signup.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/signup",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100008\"}",
      "writes": true
    },
    {
      "name": "moving onto a number somebody else has",
      "feature": "user.phone_change",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/token?grant_type=password",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100000\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\"}",
      "writes": true,
      "holds": {"mover": "body:/access_token"},
      "note": "the sign in this chain needs, kept as its own case so the refusal after it is asked by somebody the server let in",
      "volatile": [
        "/access_token",
        "/refresh_token",
        "/expires_at",
        "/user/last_sign_in_at",
        "/user/updated_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/user/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "the number that is taken",
      "feature": "user.phone_change",
      "method": "PUT",
      "path": "/auth/v1/user",
      "key": "anon",
      "headers": {
        "content-type": "application/json",
        "authorization": "Bearer {mover}"
      },
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100006\"}",
      "chained": true
    },

    {
      "name": "an operator makes an account for a number",
      "feature": "admin.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/admin/users",
      "key": "service",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100007\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\",\"phone_confirm\":true}",
      "writes": true,
      "volatile": [
        "/id",
        "/created_at",
        "/updated_at",
        "/confirmed_at",
        "/phone_confirmed_at",
        "/user_metadata/sub",
        "/identities/0/identity_id",
        "/identities/0/id",
        "/identities/0/user_id",
        "/identities/0/identity_data/sub",
        "/identities/0/last_sign_in_at",
        "/identities/0/created_at",
        "/identities/0/updated_at"
      ],
      "sorted": ["/factors"]
    },
    {
      "name": "an operator makes an account for a number somebody has",
      "feature": "admin.phone",
      "method": "POST",
      "path": "/auth/v1/admin/users",
      "key": "service",
      "headers": {"content-type": "application/json"},
      "body": "{\"phone\":\"15550100000\",\"password\":\"conformance-password\",\"phone_confirm\":true}",
      "writes": true
    }
  ]
}
